{"id":"mahabharata-12-215","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":215,"title":"पञ्चदशाधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 215 · Prahlada and Indra: the mind that is at peace","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks how deeds good and bad bring their fruit, and Bhishma tells how Indra, in the form of a brahmin, asked the fallen Prahlada how he remained calm. Prahlada answers that he neither grieves nor rejoices, since time brings all things.","kn":"ಶುಭಾಶುಭ ಕರ್ಮ ಫಲ ಹೇಗೆ ಕೊಡುತ್ತವೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣ ರೂಪದ ಇಂದ್ರ ಬಿದ್ದ ಪ್ರಹ್ಲಾದನನ್ನು ಅವನು ಶಾಂತನಾಗಿ ಹೇಗೆ ಇದ್ದಾನೆಂದು ಕೇಳಿದುದನ್ನು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕಾಲ ಎಲ್ಲವನ್ನೂ ತರುವುದರಿಂದ ತಾನು ದುಃಖಿಸುವುದಿಲ್ಲ, ಹಿಗ್ಗುವುದಿಲ್ಲವೆಂದು ಪ್ರಹ್ಲಾದ ಉತ್ತರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर पूछते हैं कि शुभ-अशुभ कर्म फल कैसे देते हैं, और भीष्म बताते हैं कि ब्राह्मण रूप इन्द्र ने पतित प्रह्लाद से पूछा कि वह शान्त कैसे रहता है। प्रह्लाद उत्तर देता है कि वह न शोक करता है न हर्ष, क्योंकि काल सब कुछ लाता है।","te":"మంచి చెడు కర్మలు ఫలాలు ఎలా ఇస్తాయని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు; బ్రాహ్మణ రూప ఇంద్రుడు పతనమైన ప్రహ్లాదుని అతడు ప్రశాంతంగా ఎలా ఉన్నాడని అడిగిన తీరును భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు. కాలం అన్నీ తెస్తుందని, తాను దుఃఖించనని, సంతోషించనని ప్రహ్లాదుడు బదులిస్తాడు.","ta":"நல்வினை தீவினை எவ்வாறு பலன் தருகின்றன என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, அந்தணர் வடிவில் இந்திரன் வீழ்ந்த பிரகலாதனிடம் அவன் எவ்வாறு அமைதியாக இருக்கிறான் என்று கேட்டதைப் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். காலம் எல்லாவற்றையும் தருகிறது, அதனால் வருந்தவோ மகிழவோ மாட்டேன் என்கிறான் பிரகலாதன்.","ml":"നല്ലതും ചീത്തയുമായ പ്രവൃത്തികൾ ഫലം നൽകുന്നതെങ്ങനെയെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; ബ്രാഹ്മണവേഷത്തിലെത്തിയ ഇന്ദ്രൻ, വീണുപോയ പ്രഹ്ലാദനോട് അദ്ദേഹം എങ്ങനെ ശാന്തനായിരിക്കുന്നുവെന്ന് ചോദിച്ചതെങ്ങനെയെന്ന് ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു. കാലം എല്ലാം കൊണ്ടുവരുന്നതിനാൽ താൻ ദുഃഖിക്കുന്നില്ലെന്നും സന്തോഷിക്കുന്നില്ലെന്നും പ്രഹ്ലാദൻ മറുപടി പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.215; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"यदिदं कर्म लोकेऽस्मिञ्शुभं वा यदि वाशुभम् ।\nपुरुषं योजयत्येव फलयोगेन भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, this action in the world, whether good or bad, binds a person to its fruit."}},{"n":2,"text":"कर्ता स्वित्तस्य पुरुष उताहो नेति संशयः ।\nएतदिच्छामि तत्त्वेन त्वत्तः श्रोतुं पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Is the person the doer of it or not? That is my doubt, grandfather; I wish to hear the truth of this from you."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"अत्राप्युदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nप्रह्रादस्य च संवादमिन्द्रस्य च युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this they tell this ancient account, Yudhishthira, the conversation of Prahlada and Indra."}},{"n":4,"text":"असक्तं धूतपाप्मानं कुले जातं बहुश्रुतम् ।\nअस्तम्भमनहंकारं सत्त्वस्थं समये रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Prahlada was unattached, free of sin, high-born, much learned, without rigidity or ego, established in sattva and fond of the rules."}},{"n":5,"text":"तुल्यनिन्दास्तुतिं दान्तं शून्यागारनिवेशनम् ।\nचराचराणां भूतानां विदितप्रभवाप्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He took blame and praise alike, was self-controlled, dwelt in empty houses, and knew the origin and dissolution of all moving and unmoving beings."}},{"n":6,"text":"अक्रुध्यन्तमहृष्यन्तमप्रियेषु प्रियेषु च ।\nकाञ्चने वाथ लोष्टे वा उभयोः समदर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was neither angry nor glad at the unpleasant or pleasant, and saw gold and a clod of earth as equal."}},{"n":7,"text":"आत्मनिःश्रेयसज्ञाने धीरं निश्चितनिश्चयम् ।\nपरावरज्ञं भूतानां सर्वज्ञं समदर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Steady in knowledge of his own highest good, firm in his resolve, knowing the high and low of beings, all-knowing, seeing all alike,"}},{"n":8,"text":"शक्रः प्रह्रादमासीनमेकान्ते संयतेन्द्रियम् ।\nबुभुत्समानस्तत्प्रज्ञामभिगम्येदमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Indra, wishing to know his wisdom, approached Prahlada sitting alone with his senses controlled, and said this."}},{"n":9,"text":"यैः कैश्चित्संमतो लोके गुणैः स्यात्पुरुषो नृषु ।\nभवत्यनपगान्सर्वांस्तान्गुणाँल्लक्षयामहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"By whatever qualities a man is esteemed among men in the world, we see all those qualities in you, undiminished."}},{"n":10,"text":"अथ ते लक्ष्यते बुद्धिः समा बालजनैरिह ।\nआत्मानं मन्यमानः सञ्श्रेयः किमिह मन्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet your outlook here appears the same as that of foolish people. Thinking yourself good, what do you take to be the highest good here?"}},{"n":11,"text":"बद्धः पाशैश्च्युतः स्थानाद्द्विषतां वशमागतः ।\nश्रिया विहीनः प्रह्राद शोचितव्ये न शोचसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bound in fetters, fallen from your place, come under the power of your foes, deprived of fortune, Prahlada, you do not grieve where grief is due."}},{"n":12,"text":"प्रज्ञालाभात्तु दैतेय उताहो धृतिमत्तया ।\nप्रह्राद स्वस्थरूपोऽसि पश्यन्व्यसनमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Is it from gaining wisdom, son of Diti, or from steadiness, Prahlada, that you stay composed while seeing your own calamity?"}},{"n":13,"text":"इति संचोदितस्तेन धीरो निश्चितनिश्चयः ।\nउवाच श्लक्ष्णया वाचा स्वां प्रज्ञामनुवर्णयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus urged by him, the steadfast Prahlada, firm in resolve, answered in gentle words, explaining his wisdom."}},{"n":14,"text":"प्रवृत्तिं च निवृत्तिं च भूतानां यो न बुध्यते ।\nतस्य स्तम्भो भवेद्बाल्यान्नास्ति स्तम्भोऽनुपश्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whoever does not understand the engagement and withdrawal of beings has rigidity from childishness; for one who sees, there is no rigidity."}},{"n":15,"text":"स्वभावात्संप्रवर्तन्ते निवर्तन्ते तथैव च ।\nसर्वे भावास्तथाभावाः पुरुषार्थो न विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"By nature all things arise and likewise cease; all conditions are of this kind, and there is no human endeavour."}},{"n":16,"text":"पुरुषार्थस्य चाभावे नास्ति कश्चित्स्वकारकः ।\nस्वयं तु कुर्वतस्तस्य जातु मानो भवेदिह ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the absence of human endeavour no one is his own maker; yet one who acts of himself might sometimes feel pride here."}},{"n":17,"text":"यस्तु कर्तारमात्मानं मन्यते साध्वसाधुनोः ।\nतस्य दोषवती प्रज्ञा स्वमूर्त्यज्ञेति मे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whoever thinks of himself as the doer of good and bad, his understanding is faulty; he is ignorant of his own form, I believe."}},{"n":18,"text":"यदि स्यात्पुरुषः कर्ता शक्रात्मश्रेयसे ध्रुवम् ।\nआरम्भास्तस्य सिध्येरन्न च जातु पराभवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If, Indra, a man were the doer, then surely his undertakings for his own good would succeed and he would never be defeated."}},{"n":19,"text":"अनिष्टस्य हि निर्वृत्तिरनिवृत्तिः प्रियस्य च ।\nलक्ष्यते यतमानानां पुरुषार्थस्ततः कुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the avoidance of the unwanted and the failure to attain the wanted are seen even among those who strive; so where is human endeavour?"}},{"n":20,"text":"अनिष्टस्याभिनिर्वृत्तिमिष्टसंवृत्तिमेव च ।\nअप्रयत्नेन पश्यामः केषांचित्तत्स्वभावतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We see in some, without effort, the avoidance of the unwanted and the gaining of the wanted, by their nature."}},{"n":21,"text":"प्रतिरूपधराः केचिद्दृश्यन्ते बुद्धिसत्तमाः ।\nविरूपेभ्योऽल्पबुद्धिभ्यो लिप्समाना धनागमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some highly intelligent people are seen, handsome in form, seeking to gain wealth from the ugly and dull-witted."}},{"n":22,"text":"स्वभावप्रेरिताः सर्वे निविशन्ते गुणा यदा ।\nशुभाशुभास्तदा तत्र तस्य किं मानकारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When all qualities, good and bad, enter a person driven by nature, what ground for pride would he have?"}},{"n":23,"text":"स्वभावादेव तत्सर्वमिति मे निश्चिता मतिः ।\nआत्मप्रतिष्ठिता प्रज्ञा मम नास्ति ततोऽन्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"My conviction is fixed that all this is from nature alone; my wisdom rests in the self and has no other view."}},{"n":24,"text":"कर्मजं त्विह मन्येऽहं फलयोगं शुभाशुभम् ।\nकर्मणां विषयं कृत्स्नमहं वक्ष्यामि तच्छृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet I hold that here the joining of good and bad fruit arises from action. I will explain the whole scope of actions; hear it."}},{"n":25,"text":"यथा वेदयते कश्चिदोदनं वायसो वदन् ।\nएवं सर्वाणि कर्माणि स्वभावस्यैव लक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As someone speaks of rice while a crow caws, so all actions are only a mark of nature."}},{"n":26,"text":"विकारानेव यो वेद न वेद प्रकृतिं पराम् ।\nतस्य स्तम्भो भवेद्बाल्यान्नास्ति स्तम्भोऽनुपश्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who knows only the transformations and not the higher nature has rigidity from childishness; for one who sees, there is no rigidity."}},{"n":27,"text":"स्वभावभाविनो भावान्सर्वानेवेह निश्चये ।\nबुध्यमानस्य दर्पो वा मानो वा किं करिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one who understands that all things here come about by nature, what can pride or arrogance do?"}},{"n":28,"text":"वेद धर्मविधिं कृत्स्नं भूतानां चाप्यनित्यताम् ।\nतस्माच्छक्र न शोचामि सर्वं ह्येवेदमन्तवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I know the whole rule of dharma and the impermanence of beings; therefore, Indra, I do not grieve, for all this has an end."}},{"n":29,"text":"निर्ममो निरहंकारो निरीहो मुक्तबन्धनः ।\nस्वस्थोऽव्यपेतः पश्यामि भूतानां प्रभवाप्ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Free of possessiveness and ego, without desire, released from bonds, composed and unwavering, I see the arising and passing of beings."}},{"n":30,"text":"कृतप्रज्ञस्य दान्तस्य वितृष्णस्य निराशिषः ।\nनायासो विद्यते शक्र पश्यतो लोकविद्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one of settled wisdom, self-controlled, free of craving and hope, who sees by the knowledge of the world, Indra, there is no toil."}},{"n":31,"text":"प्रकृतौ च विकारे च न मे प्रीतिर्न च द्विषे ।\nद्वेष्टारं न च पश्यामि यो ममाद्य ममायते ॥","meaning":{"en":"In nature and in its change, I have neither love nor hatred; and I see no hater, nor one who treats me as his own today."}},{"n":32,"text":"नोर्ध्वं नावाङ्न तिर्यक्च न क्वचिच्छक्र कामये ।\nन विज्ञाने न विज्ञेये नाज्ञाने शर्म विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I wish for nothing above, below or across, Indra; there is no peace in knowledge, in the knowable, or in ignorance."}},{"text":"शक्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Indra said:"}},{"n":33,"text":"येनैषा लभ्यते प्रज्ञा येन शान्तिरवाप्यते ।\nप्रब्रूहि तमुपायं मे सम्यक्प्रह्राद पृच्छते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell me, Prahlada, as I ask, the means by which this wisdom is gained and by which peace is attained."}},{"text":"प्रह्राद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Prahlada said:"}},{"n":34,"text":"आर्जवेनाप्रमादेन प्रसादेनात्मवत्तया ।\nवृद्धशुश्रूषया शक्र पुरुषो लभते महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By uprightness, carefulness, serenity, self-possession and service to elders, Indra, a man gains greatness."}},{"n":35,"text":"स्वभावाल्लभते प्रज्ञां शान्तिमेति स्वभावतः ।\nस्वभावादेव तत्सर्वं यत्किंचिदनुपश्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"By nature one gains wisdom, and by nature one reaches peace; all that you see is from nature alone."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":36,"text":"इत्युक्तो दैत्यपतिना शक्रो विस्मयमागमत् ।\nप्रीतिमांश्च तदा राजंस्तद्वाक्यं प्रत्यपूजयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Addressed thus by the lord of the Daityas, Indra was astonished; pleased then, O king, he honoured those words."}},{"n":37,"text":"स तदाभ्यर्च्य दैत्येन्द्रं त्रैलोक्यपतिरीश्वरः ।\nअसुरेन्द्रमुपामन्त्र्य जगाम स्वं निवेशनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, having honoured the lord of the Daityas, the sovereign of the three worlds took leave of the king of the asuras and went to his own dwelling."}}]}]}